{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat .flow/tasks/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces.5.md && rg -n -A85 '\"'^## Acceptance (Criteria|criteria|$)'\"' .flow/specs/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nsatisfies: [R6]\n---\n# fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces.5 Share plan and explore parsing directly and move semantic normalization to Runner\n\n## Description\nStage 3, second half of R6. `gomad plan` re-enters `runExplore` through a hidden flag, and application rules live in both the CLI and Runner validation. Parse once, invoke each operation directly, and leave semantic normalization with the options owner from task 2.\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** `tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/cli.go`, `explore_output.go`, `cli_test.go`, `tools/gomad3/runner/` options owner (task 2) for any normalization that moves.\n**Touches:** [tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/**, tools/gomad3/runner/*.go]\n\n### Approach\n- Hidden route: `runPlan` (`cli.go:689-691`) calls `runExplore(append([]string{\"--__plan\", \"--on-failure=all\"}, arguments...))`; `runExplore` (`:405-687`) branches on `*planOnly` at `:633`. Split `runExplore` into one shared parse step returning a typed parsed request and two thin operations (`runner.Explore`, `runner.CreateCampaignPlan`). The `--__plan` flag disappears; `gomad explore --__plan` must become an unknown-flag error, and `gomad plan` keeps `--on-failure=all` as its fixed policy with the same messages (`\"gomad plan requires --output FILE\"`, `:635`).\n- Division of rules: the CLI keeps flag-presence validation and presentation (`exploreStrategyOptions` `:693-716`, `resolveExploreStrategy` `:718-800`, `resolveExploreGuidance` `:806`, `resolveExploreSeeds` `:825`, `resolveExploreCoverage` `:841`, `resolveChoiceTrace` `:858`, and the `--coverage` needs `--choices` check `:585-594`). Semantic rules that do not depend on flag presence move to, or are deleted in favour of, Runner's normalization (`validateConfig`, `runner.go:1194`). Keep first-error precedence: for each input in the characterization table the same message wins.\n- Reuse the application value from task 4 for identity and child commands.\n- Pin behaviour with task 4's characterization tests plus plan-specific cases: `plan` with and without `--output`, JSON and text output (`:647-659`), rejected explore-only flags, and argv after the target.\n\n### Investigation targets\n**Required:**\n- `tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/cli.go:405-870`\n- `tools/gomad3/runner/runner.go:1194-1404` and the task 2 options owner\n- `tools/gomad3/runner/portable_plan.go:1-140` (`CampaignPlanSpec`, `CreateCampaignPlan`)\n- `tools/gomad3/CLI.md` (plan and explore sections)\n\n### Quick commands\n```bash\ncd tools/gomad3\nenv -u GOMADSEED -u GOMAD3_CHILD_SEED GOWORK=off .toolchain/bin/go test -count=1 -tags test_dep ./cmd/gomad/...\nenv -u GOMADSEED -u GOMAD3_CHILD_SEED GOWORK=off .toolchain/bin/go test -count=1 -tags test_dep ./runner -run 'ValidateConfig|CampaignPlan|PortablePlan'\nenv -u GOMADSEED -u GOMAD3_CHILD_SEED GOWORK=off .toolchain/bin/go test -count=1 -tags test_dep ./cmd/... ./runner/... ./qualification/...\n```\n\n### Constraints\n- No `git add`, commit, stash or worktree: the user owns commits. Record `\"commits\": []` in the `flowctl done` evidence and say so in the summary.\n- No new third-party dependency. `tools/gomad3/go.mod` requires only `golang.org/x/mod`, so testify is unavailable inside `tools/gomad3`: follow the existing `t.Fatalf` style with whole-value comparisons there. In the root module (`tools/gomad3sim`, `tools/gomad3integration`) use `require` with `Equal`/`EqualValues`.\n- Preserve existing comments with their owning code, CLI grammar/defaults, canonical bytes for fixed supplied identities, and error precedence/classification.\n- This host is `darwin/arm64`. `linux/amd64` gates cannot run here: list them as incomplete in the done summary, never claim them.\n- fn-105 D12/D14 replay-divergence dispositions stay unchanged. Attribute a failure to those owners with retained evidence instead of relaxing an expectation.\n- Run tests with `-tags test_dep`. Baseline the Quick commands before editing so a pre-existing failure is not attributed to this task.\n- Evidence and decision records go under `.flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/`.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Plan and explore share one parse step and each calls its own Runner operation; no hidden plan-only argument route remains, and `--__plan` is rejected as an unknown flag.\n- [ ] Semantic normalization has one owner in Runner; the CLI keeps only presence-sensitive validation and reporting.\n- [ ] The characterization tests from task 4 plus the plan cases pass with identical messages, classifications, stdout/stderr routing and exit statuses.\n- [ ] No default changes; explicit zero and irrelevant flags are rejected exactly as before.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n213:## Acceptance Criteria\n214-\n215-- **R1:** Local and isolated campaigns use one normalized options owner.\n216-  `MaxForcedDecisions`, `MaxExplorationResultBytes` and every\n217-  `SimulationDimensionLimits` field survive coordinator transport. Tests\n218-  exercise seed, choice and simulation strategies through actual isolated\n219-  execution with distinguishable nonzero limits. Errors: invalid/missing bounds,\n220-  incompatible strategy settings, malformed requests and unknown fields remain\n221-  rejected; local fake-executor tests alone do not fulfill transport coverage.\n222-  [paraphrase]\n223-- **R2:** Seed, choice and simulation completion use fn-108's shared private\n224-  computational assessment. Fixed-input projections and classifications match\n225-  the pre-extraction behavior. Errors: malformed/missing World evidence, wrong\n226-  seed, coverage/choice errors, watchdog, cancellation and simultaneous faults\n227-  preserve precedence and strategy-specific effects. Fulfilled through fn-108\n228-  R6 with linked evidence. [paraphrase]\n229-- **R3:** Shared retention and artifact composition hide novelty, capacities\n230-  and payload assembly while preserving seed, round and corpus transactions.\n231-  Errors: duplicate failures, incomplete transcripts, count/byte exhaustion,\n232-  publication failure, cancelled/interrupted commits and failed corpus replay\n233-  preserve bounded evidence and committed policy state. Fulfilled through\n234-  fn-108 R7 with linked evidence. [paraphrase]\n235-- **R4:** Explore, portable planning, analysis and compatibility review use one\n236-  complete preparation owner returning validated target/review evidence with\n237-  adapter identities attached. Workspace cleanup is owned explicitly. Tests\n238-  cover fresh/cache builds, external modules/local replacements, custom\n239-  preparers and independent qualification preparations. Errors: invalid sums,\n240-  replacement conflicts, unsupported closure, malformed linked records,\n241-  changed binaries and cleanup failures retain classifications. Closure\n242-  inspection does not compile or execute. [paraphrase]\n243-- **R5:** Public executor injection moves behind private dependencies, with all\n244-  repository consumers migrated and supported external use compiled from\n245-  outside the Runner subtree. Keep usable preparation/replay seams and fake\n246-  failure coverage through private adapters. Errors: inaccessible internal\n247-  types, global mutable test hooks and exposed descriptor mechanics fail\n248-  acceptance; execution failures retain existing semantics. Fulfills D3.\n249-  [paraphrase]\n250-- **R6:** CLI operation construction resolves installation/private modes once\n251-  and shares semantic normalization with Runner. Plan and explore share parsing\n252-  directly. Tests cover documented command grammar, explicit zero/irrelevant\n253-  flags, environment/tags/argv, text/JSON output and exit statuses. Errors:\n254-  malformed input and output-writer failures retain existing behavior; a\n255-  changed default or hidden plan-only argument route fails acceptance.\n256-  [paraphrase]\n257-- **R7:** Simulation-time layout and codecs have one generated definition with\n258-  host and runtime-safe consumers. Cross-consumer vectors preserve bytes and\n259-  exercise actual runtime consumption on both platforms. Errors: truncated\n260-  frames, wrong magic/kind, nonzero reserved bytes, generation mismatch and\n261-  time regression fail as before. Generated-output drift fails validation.\n262-  [paraphrase]\n263-- **R8:** Architecture checks discover every host package on both qualified\n264-  source sets and enforce targeted ownership, host-effect and public-signature\n265-  visibility rules. Negative fixtures demonstrate rejection of an ownerless\n266-  new root, forbidden effect/import edge and inaccessible public type. Valid\n267-  platform files and explicit overlay/fixture exclusions remain accepted.\n268-  Errors: silently uninspected packages and checks based only on filename\n269-  presence fail acceptance. Fulfills D4. [paraphrase]\n270-- **R9:** Current architectural guidance describes both supported platforms,\n271-  implemented choice replay/exploration and both backends, using existing\n272-  requirement IDs. Separate capability support, repeatability, exact replay\n273-  and expectation matching. Document current residual findings and intentional\n274-  Go interface changes. Errors: unmeasured support or performance claims,\n275-  obsolete delivery-state claims and failures described as qualification\n276-  success fail acceptance. Fulfills D5. [paraphrase]\n277-- **R10:** Target compilation, Go identity queries and listing use a coherent\n278-  private host-command seam with contextual lifetime and output limits. Tests\n279-  cover command cancellation/termination, long diagnostics and cache-lock\n280-  release. Errors: structured-output overflow, malformed listing, unsupported\n281-  capability, timeout and cleanup failure stay distinct; truncated structured\n282-  data cannot be accepted. [paraphrase]\n283-- **R11:** Compare at least two simulation-progress interfaces and implement\n284-  the chosen lifecycle owner, removing caller-owned multi-counter sequencing\n285-  and duplicate response-barrier bookkeeping. Tests cover forwarding,\n286-  acknowledged arrivals, delivered-but-unconsumed work, arrival at quiescence,\n287-  cancellation with late committed response, death and restart. Errors:\n288-  unknown acknowledgement, abandoned response and stale incarnation fail\n289-  before invalid progress or model mutation; concurrent blocking operations\n290-  remain possible. Design evidence alone leaves this requirement unmet.\n291-  [paraphrase]\n292-- **R12:** Network and filesystem factories select backend-specific handles\n293-  once, with private implementations owning valid local/process state.\n294-  Shared operation tests cover standalone and both simulation backends;\n295-  backend-specific tests retain hard-isolation and mapping distinctions.\n296-  Errors: duplicate bind, deadline, close/reset, partial I/O, capacity, stale\n297-  incarnation and replay divergence preserve behavior and validation-before-\n298-  mutation. Moving dispatch into another forwarding helper alone does not\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
