{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'plan|--on-failure|--output|--__plan' tools/gomad3/CLI.md | head -85 && cat .flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-5/final-plan-output.log && cat .flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-5/semantic-runner.log && cat .flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-5/semantic-cli.log\"","aggregated_output":"22:                 plan -> execute-shard -> merge\n124:The default failure policy stops after the first retained failure. Use `--on-failure=budget --failure-budget=N` to stop after N distinct failure signatures, or `--on-failure=all` to finish the complete selection.\n143:`--diagnostics` on `explore` and `plan` records runtime-state diagnostics and implies `--choices`; it accepts only `--strategy=seed` and rejects forced-prefix exploration. Diagnostic traces support locating differences between fresh executions. They do not establish exact replay.\n145:Choice recording defaults to 8 MiB and accepts at most `--choice-bytes=64MiB`; overflow fails visibly. Output retention defaults to 8 MiB per stream, adjustable with `--output-limit`. Deterministic I/O transcript capacity defaults to 64 MiB and accepts `--io-transcript-bytes` from 64 MiB through 1 GiB in whole MiB increments. A larger transcript does not increase choice capacity.\n196:`--choice-start-ordinal=N` expands only replay-plan decisions at ordinal N or later, while retaining earlier decisions in each forced prefix. The default is 0. Find the ordinals with `inspect --choices`; resume restores the recorded start ordinal. Using this flag with seed or Combined Exploration is invalid input. Select polls with fewer than two ready cases are recorded but do not expand the Frontier; results report their omitted alternatives separately.\n305:  --output=.gomad/qualification-report.json \\\n319:    --output=.gomad/qualification-shard-${shard%/*}.json \\\n324:  --output=.gomad/qualification-report.json \\\n349:## Step 6: distribute a campaign with `plan`, `execute-shard`, and `merge`\n351:The local workflow is trustworthy, but the seed set is too large for one host. Freeze a supported seed Campaign into a portable plan:\n354:tools/gomad3/.bin/gomad plan \\\n356:  --output=campaign.plan.json \\\n360:`plan` packages the verified Prepared Target, complete selection, identities, bounds, environment, and captured read-only inputs. The portable format accepts seed Campaigns and fixes the failure policy to complete all planned work. Guided plans freeze the corpus snapshot, selection, and regression mode; shards execute that selection without opening or updating the live corpus.\n362:Workers must match the plan's platform and recorded toolchain, Runner, boundary, adapter, and compatibility-pack identities. Portability distributes work among compatible workers; it does not make a target binary portable across architectures or operating systems.\n367:tools/gomad3/.bin/gomad execute-shard --shard=0/4 campaign.plan.json\n368:tools/gomad3/.bin/gomad execute-shard --shard=1/4 campaign.plan.json\n369:tools/gomad3/.bin/gomad execute-shard --shard=2/4 campaign.plan.json\n370:tools/gomad3/.bin/gomad execute-shard --shard=3/4 campaign.plan.json\n377:  --output=.gomad/merged-campaign \\\n378:  campaign.plan.json \\\n385:`merge` rejects mixed plans, overlapping ordinals, unexplained gaps, corrupt evidence, and aggregate capacity overflow. It deduplicates retained evidence by content and never mutates shard Campaigns. Use `--partial` only when publishing an explicitly incomplete aggregate is the intended result; missing ordinal ranges remain visible.\n451:  --output=tools/gomad3integration/qualification/tests.json\n542:  --output=internal/compatibilitypack/reports/PACK.md\n635:| `inspect` | Validate and explain plans, Campaigns, aggregates, and Artifacts. |\n642:| `plan` | Freeze a supported seed Campaign into a portable bundle. |\n643:| `execute-shard` | Execute one deterministic shard of a portable plan. |\nok  \tgo.temporal.io/server/tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad\t3.889s\nok  \tgo.temporal.io/server/tools/gomad3/runner\t0.874s\nok  \tgo.temporal.io/server/tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli\t0.355s\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
